feat(growth): public demo at /try + onboarding polish

Add a public, no-signup interactive demo and improve first-run
onboarding to lift top-of-funnel conversion.

Demo page (/try, also /demo redirect):
- New standalone DemoPage rendered outside AppShell (public route).
- Three-pane sandbox: dataset list, customer data table preview,
  AI assistant with three scripted insights (spend by region,
  top customers, monthly signups).
- Real interactive echarts charts driven from in-memory data.
- All save / export / connect-source actions show a sign-up
  gate modal listing what unlocks: own files, DB connectors,
  saved checkpoints, scheduled pipelines, sharing.
- Sticky top bar + sandbox banner with persistent "Sign up free"
  CTAs.
- Fully responsive (desktop 3-col -> tablet 2-col -> mobile 1-col).
- New PostHog events: demo_viewed, demo_insight_selected,
  demo_signup_gate_shown, demo_signup_clicked, demo_login_clicked.

Homepage:
- Add a "Try a live demo - no signup required" pill link directly
  under the hero CTAs to capture visitors not ready to commit.
- Fires homepage_try_demo_clicked for funnel attribution.

Onboarding (WelcomeModal):
- Promote a new Customers sample (30 rows) as the Quickstart
  default - smaller, more universal than the GL sample for
  first-time activation.
- Tighten copy: "From CSV to chart in under 60 seconds."
- Step 1 wording shifted to "Pick a sample (or upload)" to lower
  the activation bar.
- New welcome-modal sample-badge styling for the Quickstart pill.

Assets:
- Add samples/customers.csv (30 rows) and mirror it under
  frontend/public/samples/ so WelcomeModal can fetch it.

No backend or auth changes. Demo page makes zero API calls.
